WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.459
Wherever there's an ocean, there's

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:02.794
going to be some big empire

00:00:02.794 --> 00:00:03.962
that wants to control it.

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:05.130
But there's one ocean,

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.047
up at the top of the world

00:00:06.047 --> 00:00:07.590
that hasn't ever been controlled

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.717
by great powers

00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:09.426
because it's

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:11.302
literally frozen most of the time.

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:11.845
But that’s changing

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.221
because up here in the Arctic,

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:15.473
things are heating up four times

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:17.100
faster than the rest of the planet.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.228
And some big countries see a lot of money

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:22.564
and influence hiding under the ice.

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:24.149
There are deposits of fossil fuels.

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:25.692
Shipping routes. And minerals.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:26.526
So what it's turned into

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.236
is all of these countries: Russia,

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:29.612
the United States, and even China,

00:00:29.612 --> 00:00:30.905
who's not even an Arctic country,

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:31.740
but kind of wants to

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.574
be an Arctic country.

00:00:32.574 --> 00:00:33.199
But just isn't.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.576
All of them are now vying

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:36.036
for influence in the Arctic.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:36.995
Greenland belongs

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:38.038
to the kingdom of Denmark.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.831
They are a member of the military

00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:40.915
alliance called NATO.

00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:41.291
The U.S.

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:42.876
even has a military base up here.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.045
But Greenland is also kind of tied

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:45.712
to China.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.297
A lot of their economy relies

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:49.007
on sending fish to China.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:50.967
The result of all of this is tension.

00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:52.427
More and more every year.

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:53.970
I actually went to Greenland

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:54.429
to try

00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:55.263
to understand

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:57.307
what this really important island

00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:58.683
means for the future of

00:00:58.683 --> 00:00:59.976
influence in the Arctic.

